Rāma with Sītā gives wealth and goes to see his father --- Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa take wondrous garlanded bows --- Citizens crown roofs and towers to gaze in grief --- People lament Rāma on foot without umbrella and the army once following him --- People praise truthful Rāma refusing falsehood for his father --- People grieve sky-unseen Sītā now exposed on royal road --- People blame possessed Daśaratha for exiling virtuous Rāma --- People vow to follow him leaving gardens houses and city a forest for Kaikēyī --- People declare the forest a city where Rāma goes --- Rāma hears varied voices unmoved and seeks his father through Sumantra
